@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy"; }
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="section-kicker">Privacy and exam data</span><h1>How the system uses examination data.</h1><p>Read this information before creating an account or starting an examination.</p></div></section>
<section class="public-section bg-white"><div class="container privacy-content">
    <h2>Information collected</h2><p>The system may store account details, CNIC, Candidate ID, profile and verification photos, exam answers, marks, security events and short evidence files.</p>
    <h2>Why it is used</h2><p>The information is used to manage accounts, confirm eligibility, deliver and mark exams, review monitoring events, provide support and protect the system.</p>
    <h2>Camera and microphone</h2><p>The browser asks for permission before using the camera or microphone. Entire Screen sharing is not requested. Face Identity Model 1 sends fresh camera frames to the local verification service; its Python service stores accepted enrollment photos and biometric references privately. Students can view their own photos; authorized administrators can reset enrollment, deleting the saved photos and references.</p>
    <h2>Human review and fairness</h2><p>Future AI observations will not be treated as automatic proof of misconduct. Lighting, disability, camera angle, device quality, speech recognition and network conditions must be considered through authorized review and a suitable appeal route.</p>
    <h2>Who can view evidence</h2><p>Monitoring evidence is kept outside the public web folder and can be opened only through authorized Teacher or Administrator pages.</p>
    <h2>Institution responsibility</h2><p>Before real use, the institution should publish its approved privacy policy, retention period, appeal process and contact details, and follow applicable Pakistani requirements.</p>
</div></section>
